From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:53:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] yblod-61: one type in the HDR10+ flags conditional

DVVK_HDR10PLUS_V1 is an enumerator and 0u an unsigned int, so the
conditional that sets playbackHDR10PlusFlags mixed an enumerated and a
non-enumerated type, the one -Wextra warning in the fork's code. Cast
the enumerator to the atomic's uint32_t; the value stored is the same.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index 89df288..63b6c84 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -1291,7 +1291,8 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::BeginDVBridge()
   const bool tunnelHDR10Plus = tunnelHDR10 &&
                                DVBRIDGE::playbackMode.load() == DVBRIDGE::OutputMode::HDR10Plus &&
                                SupportsTunnelHDR10Plus();
-  DVBRIDGE::playbackHDR10PlusFlags.store(DisplayHDR10PlusVersion() >= 1 ? DVVK_HDR10PLUS_V1 : 0u);
+  DVBRIDGE::playbackHDR10PlusFlags.store(
+      DisplayHDR10PlusVersion() >= 1 ? static_cast<uint32_t>(DVVK_HDR10PLUS_V1) : 0u);
   const bool plusChanged = DVBRIDGE::playbackTunnelHDR10Plus.exchange(tunnelHDR10Plus) != tunnelHDR10Plus;
   if (DVBRIDGE::playbackTunnelHDR10.exchange(tunnelHDR10) != tunnelHDR10 || plusChanged)
     CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "DVBridge output: {}", tunnelHDR10Plus
